00:38:00.440 --> 00:38:04.500
Well, it must be something good, because you ain't stood in the driveway waiting for me since I brought you on my bicycle.

00:38:05.290 --> 00:38:06.090
What the hell is this?

00:38:08.680 --> 00:38:10.340
You're Mark Taggart. We're pleased to inform you.

00:38:10.400 --> 00:38:15.430
You have passed the first round of NASA examinations and are now eligible to proceed. I'll be damned.

00:38:15.650 --> 00:38:17.070
Well, it just gets me to the next round.

00:38:17.390 --> 00:38:20.960
Well, that's one round closer. Get in. I'll buy you a beer.

00:38:22.620 --> 00:38:25.220
You know, Neil was right. They asked the weirdest question about duct tape.

00:38:25.590 --> 00:38:27.150
Sometimes I think that guy's smarter than he looks.

00:38:27.840 --> 00:38:28.960
Well, with that hair, he ought to be.

00:38:30.320 --> 00:38:38.710
So we're walking along the beach in Waikiki on our honeymoon, full moon, endless sand, no one in sight.

00:38:39.360 --> 00:38:43.220
Sarah is whispering about the dress her cousin Charlene wore to the wedding.

00:38:43.680 --> 00:38:45.680
She's afraid that somebody's going to hear her.

00:38:45.780 --> 00:38:46.520
Now listen to this.

00:38:46.820 --> 00:38:52.060
I couldn't hear her, so you can damn well be sure that her cousin Charlene couldn't hear her all the way back in Detroit.

00:38:53.120 --> 00:38:59.970
No better than Miss Big Mom.

00:39:00.060 --> 00:39:00.800
What?

00:39:01.120 --> 00:39:04.460
Wait, you have at least one cousin who's not speaking to you at the moment.

00:39:04.580 --> 00:39:06.220
She got these awful extensions, okay?

00:39:06.520 --> 00:39:09.560
And I'm just... she should thank me for telling her the truth.

00:39:10.880 --> 00:39:12.200
You remember what I was mentioning?

00:39:14.260 --> 00:39:16.460
Sometimes the truth is better left unsaid.

00:39:16.640 --> 00:39:16.800
Uh-huh.

00:39:16.940 --> 00:39:18.540
You're one to talk, you're just like Ben.

00:39:20.590 --> 00:39:21.670
How do you know my father's name?

00:39:34.350 --> 00:39:35.270
Would you like some pie?

00:39:39.670 --> 00:39:41.810
I never knew the IRS could be so aggressive.

00:39:42.110 --> 00:39:43.830
You know, you steal a billion, you're a genius,

00:39:44.090 --> 00:39:45.170
and you fudge a tax return.

00:39:45.450 --> 00:39:46.730
I could have sworn one of them had a gun.

00:39:46.970 --> 00:39:48.370
It was just for show, you know.

00:39:50.730 --> 00:39:51.110
What's that?

00:39:52.200 --> 00:39:53.580
Chocolate malt lambic.

00:39:54.300 --> 00:39:55.340
I got the recipe off the internet.

00:39:55.680 --> 00:39:57.040
I used to mull my own wine,

00:39:57.140 --> 00:39:59.060
so I figured why not try my own micro-brew?

00:39:59.640 --> 00:39:59.900
Mmm.

00:40:00.440 --> 00:40:02.160
I made some Swiss smoked almond for dessert.

00:40:02.580 --> 00:40:04.840
Chocolate beer? How interesting.

00:40:05.540 --> 00:40:08.220
Put all kinds of things in beer. Hot peppers, marshmallows.

00:40:08.780 --> 00:40:09.820
Marshmallows and hot peppers.

00:40:11.380 --> 00:40:14.250
Kidding. Try keeping that down.

00:40:15.420 --> 00:40:23.560
Right. Strangely refreshing.

00:40:25.100 --> 00:40:27.340
See? I told you you'd have a good time.

00:40:27.420 --> 00:40:29.020
I never doubted it for a second.

00:40:30.890 --> 00:40:33.430
So, who was that cute little girl you were with?

00:40:33.770 --> 00:40:34.310
Oh, Stevie?

00:40:34.960 --> 00:40:36.900
Oh, she was cute, wasn't she?

00:41:00.640 --> 00:41:03.720
4, 5, 6, 7, 9, 10.

00:41:36.780 --> 00:41:37.000
Thank you.
